        {
          "id": 1251218703,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "We could do that, sure. I assumed that `g_ascii_strcasecmp()` was doing its own case-folding, which would impose its penalty for each iteration of the `for` loop, compared to once when doing it this way.\n\nAnother alternative to allocating a new string would be to iterate over the original filename string and lowercase each letter in-place, the way the now-deprecated [`g_strdown()`](https://developer-old.gnome.org/glib/stable/glib-String-Utility-Functions.html#g-strdown) did.\n\nI'm not particular about which approach we go with, so let me know your preference and I'll push an update.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6020526,
            "username": "boolean263",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "David Perry",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6020526/avatar.png?v=1789780429",
